  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "*Page type*\n\n1. Given a Site Merchandiser creates a Group with Lookbook entry in Contentful, when configuring it, then they must select a page type: PLP, Home Page, or Other (required).\n2. Given a Site Merchandiser selects PLP as the page type, when configuring the entry, then a category field becomes mandatory and they must specify the SFCC category or categories it applies to.\n\n*Number of cards*\n\n3. Given a Site Merchandiser is configuring the entry, when selecting the number of cards, then they can choose 2, 3, or 5 (required).\n\n*Card type*\n\n4. Given a Site Merchandiser is configuring each card slot, when selecting the card type, then they must choose either an editorial card (image-based/video-based) or a product card (required per slot).\n\n*Editorial card content*\n\n5. Given a Site Merchandiser has selected editorial card for a slot, when configuring it, then they can upload an image/video (required) and optionally add a title and link above the image/video\n6. Given a Site Merchandiser is configuring an editorial card, when they optionally add editorial text, then they can author a header, body copy, and an optional link.\n\n*Product card content*\n\n7. Given a Site Merchandiser has selected product card for a slot, when configuring it, then they must enter a product ID and select the product card type (Home, PLP/PDP, or Wishlist).\n\n*Preview & publishing*\n\n8. Given a Site Merchandiser has configured the entry, when they want to verify the result, then they can preview the page in Contentful before publishing.\n9. Given a Site Merchandiser publishes the entry, when it goes live, then the configured Card Group with Lookbook is visible on the relevant page.\n10. Given a Site Merchandiser unpublishes or removes the entry, when the change goes live, then the component no longer appears on the page.\n\n*Validation*\n\n11. Given a Site Merchandiser attempts to publish the entry, when any required field is empty, then Contentful prevents publishing and surfaces a validation error."
  },
